e5411b0c389063d7e99435e0301d40ada56e38","event_uuid":"80904fb7-6ab0-44a4-891e-d8790d1b0744","position":{"commit_sha":"aa614aef6701bef5f079a080c196501751ff1cdf","position":"1788517165471994001-80904fb7-6ab0-44a4-891e-d8790d1b0744"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6fd7572a060d83d48a8ba0b6b512820add20b825e3d181d703804e3e16890a13","event_uuid":"b9ccf57a-52a5-4cc9-b712-bed63f5294eb","position":{"commit_sha":"51b354b93d7392bfb083cb3f01e2f5ab2ada8dff","position":"1788517342816797001-b9ccf57a-52a5-4cc9-b712-bed63f5294eb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5f6ea8dc0064ea830cd3bd0a8bbadd8de578bb8c12817b2f7a46d70ead42016c","event_uuid":"9234a066-8803-4855-be41-05607dcf1682","position":{"commit_sha":"547595badb977bcaa067329824f6a52a37e24773","position":"1788518574851508001-9234a066-8803-4855-be41-05607dcf1682"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Epic review #2 (desc 7927c) BLOCK on T8 (new finding): inline-fixture emitter/selector assumed every mined criterion is inline-runnable, but eval_solver.py:100-140 has 3 runner paths — CONTAINER_CRITERIA (G3/G4/decomp-shape) need a children payload, ISF raises on inline fixtures; both carry a cohort tag so the selector would wrongly admit them. Remediation: added 'Only inline-runnable criteria are mined' paragraph (selector EXCLUDES container+ISF from inline mining -> self-healing loop files unreliable-criterion tickets; admission runner treats un-runnable shape as WITHHELD-with-reason); added container/ISF case to no-fire AC; fixed citations (pass1.py:283-298, plan_review/sidecar.py); compressed to 7982c under 8000 cap. Relaunched review #3 job 1788388287913034479-6f3c2e6615594cd7a2cc9bacc3a04c95.","timestamp":1788388327729112001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Epic review #3 PASSED (certified, currency_basis=file_impact). Claimed epic 65dd + fb55. fb55 (ledger cap params) implemented held-out TDD: 5 new tests in tests/unit/test_ledger_cap_params.py (RED confirmed, GREEN after impl), mutation-teeth verified under sandbox. Caught+fixed a regression to existing test_reserve_derives_cap_math_from_module_constants (default-arg bound at def-time broke live global-read) by switching cap_usd/reserve_usd to None sentinels resolved live. lint+typecheck clean. Full make test: 9 pre-existing/environmental failures (8 in tests/interfaces git-subprocess repos, 1 confirmed identical with my change stashed) + my 18797 pass. Committed b0737da (rebar-ticket fb55-04d6-4beb-4025) -> Gerrit change 2546, awaiting LLM-Review + Verified. Next: 549b selector.","timestamp":1788395384369099001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"549b (selector) plan-review #1 BLOCKed on E1/E2 (unnamed Pass-2 label signal) + G6 (verifier-vintage sub-gate failure mode). Root cause: both label signals (reproduction consensus, author-response) are Pass-1 finder observations from the historical sidecar, NOT Pass-2 verifier output, so no plan-review-verifier vintage sub-gate applies. Remediated 549b description to state this explicitly (7949 chars). Relaunching review_plan.","timestamp":1788396952176192001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"fb55 close-gate finding: the async verify_completion_start default (source=attested, ref=origin/main) FAILed because fb55's code is not yet landed on origin/main. The REAL close gate (close_autoresume.py:271) verifies against ref=HEAD (the committed worktree tree), not origin/main. Re-ran verify_completion_start(ref=HEAD) to pre-sign the HEAD-anchored attestation the close will reuse. fb55 change 2546 is LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1.","timestamp":1788397461227758001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"549b review #2 (against remediated 7949 material) still BLOCKed on 3 NEW findings: E2 (manifest had no serialization format), G6 (no-fire candidate norm_id source unspecified), G7 (no-fire direction redefined the epic's cohort/routed predicate). Resolved all three: manifest is now JSONL (sorted keys, rank order); no-fire candidates keyed (C, norm_id=None); no-fire admitted ONLY under the epic's predicate (C in some finding's cohort on the plan AND no finding cites C, missing-cohort skipped), consensus only RAISES to advisory. Also addressed blocking project.portability advisory: vintage-gate git-log resolves against gate_source.default_ref and fails closed to no-committed-prompt-history when the base ref is absent/errs. Final 7953 chars, description_warning null. Initial auto-push to origin/tickets hit a concurrent-writer race; resolved via push recovery. Relaunching review #3.","timestamp":1788398896921327001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5a