c_tier never returns DET) -> dropped DET from mapping (AGENT->agent, 1-TURN/2-STEP->cheap). Advisories: A6 align with emitter's per-criterion spec files (dataset cases carry expect), A7 run_case kw-only args, A8 reserve_usd=0 for true 250 ceiling, A2 stable run_id=admission-<prompt_id>, A4 path citations evals/, A5 retry bound (3 attempts+backoff), A1 balance-withhold AC. Desc 7982 chars, 10 ACs. Re-running review-plan round 3.","timestamp":1788419981764834001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"67aa plan-review round 3: BLOCK (1 blocker + 2 advisories). B1 [G6]: $250 cap enforced only vs pre-flight estimates via reserve(); finalize() prices ACTUAL usage and cumulative actual spend never re-checked -> a per-criterion actual over its estimate can push total past 250 undetected. FIX: after EACH finalize, re-read cumulative actual spend from ledger; if >= cap_usd, halt FATALLY before any further criterion (added AC#4 + Budget/Failure prose). A2 [G6]: strict validation also requires non-empty gold_set + >=1 deterministic gating scorer, not just balanced dataset. FIX: runner carries candidate's strict-only fields (prompt/model/epochs/gate/coverage_threshold/scorers) UNCHANGED and rebuilds dataset+gold_set from reproducing cases; withhold if filtered gold_set/dataset empty or unbalanced. Desc 7963 chars, 11 ACs (9 codebase + 2 non-codebase). Round 4 running.","timestamp":1788420948674158001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"67aa plan-review round 4: BLOCK (2 blockers). B1 [E6/E2]: referenced an 'admission report' sink for selector tier but never specified path/format/fields, no AC proving it written. FIX: dropped the phantom file entirely; runner returns an in-memory summary (admitted/withheld ids, drift entries, spend) asserted by tests; spec carries no posture/tier field (not eval-spec schema). B2 [G6]: per-criterion atomicity false - spec-file write and ledger finalize() are two unordered disk ops; crash between them corrupts resume either way (ledger-first-crash loses spec while charged; spec-first-crash leaves a spec the no-shadowing SKIP mistakes for a built-in). FIX: STRICT ORDER atomic spec os.replace FIRST then finalize() SECOND; ledger run_id is sole resume oracle; no-shadowing scoped to PACKAGED built-ins only (a same-id .rebar/evals file is a prior artifact, idempotently overwritten, never skipped). Invariant: finalized criterion always has its spec. Added crash-orphan resume AC + packaged-only skip AC. Desc 7944 chars, 11 ACs. Round 5 running.","timestamp":1788422030250258001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"67aa plan-review round 5: BLOCK (1 blocker + 2 advisories). B1 [G6]: drift-report output internally contradictory - plan both mandates a committed drift-report FILE and said 'no report file is written'. FIX: my round-4 phrase referred to the ADMISSION-SUMMARY file, not the drift report; reworded to 'the drift report and admitted specs are the only file outputs (no separate admission-summary file)'. A1 [T8]: drift entry required 'originating review' but the emitter's must-fire case carries no review-uuid - it embeds norm_id (fire) / review_event_uuid (pass) in the case input descriptor (verified in fixture_emit._input_descriptor). FIX: drift entry now cites criterion, case id, predicted/observed, and the embedded provenance id (norm_id for must-fire, review_event_uuid for must-not-fire); AC2 aligned. A2 [P6] AC/DoD quality: advisory. Desc 7981 chars, 11 ACs. Round 6 running.","timestamp":1788422789129692001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"67aa round-6 IND1 remediation: reviewer correctly caught that the emitter's case input is a model-free provenance descriptor (not plan text), so running the Pass-1 finder on 